# Components

A component is a function that takes props and returns HTML. This one
greets whoever you pass as `name`:

```rocci
@component
Hello = |{ name }|
    <p>Hello, <strong>{name}</strong></p>
```

You can use the `rocci show` command to preview the component.

```sh
rocci show Hello.rocci --arg name=Ada
```

The window should read **Hello, Ada**.

The `.rocci` file may also contain normal Roc code in addition to the template functions.


## Composing components

Component names are PascalCase. Consecutive leading capitals (`HTMLShell`)
are rejected as ambiguous; write `HtmlShell`. The generated roc functions are lowercase due to roc naming conventions.

Nested markup is a **second parameter**, not a `children` field on the
props record. A self-closing tag (`<Hello name="Ada" />`) is a one-argument
call. A paired tag (`<Card title="Hello">…</Card>`) passes the inner markup
as that second argument, typed `Html`.

Write `{content}` for that body parameter: it is already `Html`, so Rocci
inserts it as-is. Do not put the nested tree on the props record
(`|{ title, content }|`). A `{content}` interpolation in text position
expects `Str`, so an `Html` field would be wrapped in `Html.text` and
escaped (you would see tags as literal text, not nested elements).

```rocci
@component Card = |{ title }, content|
    <section>
        <h2>{title}</h2>
        {content}
    </section>

@component Page = |_|
    <Card title="Hello">
        <p>Body is Html, not a string.</p>
    </Card>
```

Qualified calls use the imported module: `<Design.Button />` becomes
`Design.button`. Missing PascalCase names fail in Roc, not in a
client-side registry.

`??` field defaults are **experimental**. Omit the field at the call
site; generated Roc uses a type-position default so Roc fills it.

A component is **pure**: given the same props and body, it produces the
same markup. It cannot log, open SQLite, or read the request. Effects
belong in `@init` and handlers. There is no runtime component registry
and no implicit instance state.

## Preview with fixtures

`@fixture` bindings feed `rocci show` and `rocci browse`. `@test`
bindings check a boolean with `rocci test`. Neither changes the generated
component function.

```rocci
@fixture{target: Hello}
helloTest = { name: "Ada" }
```

```sh
rocci show Hello.rocci
```

The preview shows **Hello, Ada** from `helloTest`. Pass `--arg name=Roc`
to override.

Put reusable widgets in `components/`. Keep page-private helpers in the
same `.rocci` module. `rocci browse components/` lists fixtures across a
directory.

The exact grammar is in
[Components](/docs/reference/language/components/).

